        <name>NPD_MEMIC_NODETYPE_SHIFT</name>
        <initializer>(28U)</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Bit position of the MEMIC node-type nibble inside an NpdMemIcAddresses[] entry. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The upper 4 bits of each NpdMemIcAddresses[] entry encode the MEMIC node type (NPS / NMU / etc.), allowing the address table to recover the node type without a parallel array. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
